{# layout.knap — the page frame. knap has no includes by design, so a page
   owns its whole frame: start a new page from a copy of this file, then add
   the route to routes.txt and write data/<name>.json with the fields this
   template reads. The head of the page (charset, title, stylesheet) is not
   knap's job — build.sh passes it to dogbed render as --title/--css. #}
{{ title | h1 }}

{{ intro }}

{{ body }}

{{ "Elsewhere" | h2 }}

* "home":index.html
* "about":about.html

rendered by "dogbed":https://github.com/drawmeanelephant/dogbed — k4o templates it, oliver renders it.
